null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06314073524688148,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":81.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.3672068393868766,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.27631,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Blue Ridge Bankshares, Inc. operates as a bank holding company for the Blue Ridge Bank, National Association that provides commercial and consumer banking, and financial services. It operates through Commercial Banking and Mortgage Banking segments. The company accepts checking, savings, money market, cash management, and individual retirement accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. It also offers commercial and industrial, residential mortgages, commercial mortgages, home equity, and consumer installment loans; and residential mortgage loans and mortgages loans on real estate. In addition, it provides commercial banking services, including deposit accounts, treasury management solutions, wire services, online banking, fraud prevention services, procurement cards, and a range of commercial lending options; and property and casualty insurance products to individuals and businesses, as well as electronic statement, and mobile and telephone banking services. Further, the company offers consumer lending services that include automobile lending, home equity lines of credit, credit cards, and other unsecured personal loans; small business administration loans; management services for personal and corporate trusts, including estate planning and settlement, trust administration, and investment and wealth management services, as well as life insurance products. It operates in Callao, Charlottesville, Chester, Colonial Heights, Culpeper, Fredericksburg, Gordonsville, Harrisonburg, Hartfield, Henrico, Kilmarnock, Louisa, Luray, Martinsville, Midlothian, Mineral, Montross, Orange, Petersburg, Richmond, Shenandoah, Suffolk, Virginia Beach, Warsaw, and White Stone, Virginia; and Greensboro, North Carolina. The company was founded in 1893 and is headquartered in Richmond, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Harry W. Golliday | Interim CEO, Interim President & Director | Age 61","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 255 people. Revenue per employee of $360K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Blue Ridge Bankshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $358M market cap on $92M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -17% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $12M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.27\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 28% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 397% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.971687466463127},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Are PAG, BRBS, PSNL Obtaining Fair Deals for their Shareholders?","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/are-pag-brbs-psnl-obtaining-fair-deals-for-their-shareholders-302924840.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793367660.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Blue Ridge Bankshares